  "summary": "Pillow: MSP RLE decoder expands a tiny file into unbounded memory",
  "details": "### Summary\nThe MSP RLE decoder expands run-length data into an in-memory buffer with no cap tied to the declared image size. A small file that passes the pixel-count check can force hundreds of megabytes or more of allocation when the application loads pixels.\n\n### Details\nThe MSP decoder writes each run into an unbounded `io.BytesIO` and can expand roughly 85x per run:\n\n- `src/PIL/MspImagePlugin.py:144-146`\n\n### Impact\nMemory-exhaustion denial of service from a tiny crafted image in any application that loads pixels. The expansion is decoupled from the declared pixel count, so `MAX_IMAGE_PIXELS` does not bound it.",
